1
00:00:05,490 --> 00:00:08,450
The problem appears to be unsolvable.

2
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,550
Maybe we could run some computer simulations.

3
00:00:10,620 --> 00:00:13,190
There are too many variables. It would take forever.

4
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:15,720
We've got to be missing something.

5
00:00:15,790 --> 00:00:17,320
Let's start again.

6
00:00:17,390 --> 00:00:21,020
The movie is playing here at 7:20, here at 7:40,

7
00:00:21,090 --> 00:00:23,620
here at 8:10 and here at 8:45.

8
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:26,030
These theaters have to be eliminated.

9
00:00:26,030 --> 00:00:28,480
Why? They're state-of-the-art digital projection,

10
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:29,570
20-channel surround sound.

11
00:00:29,570 --> 00:00:33,170
Yes, but they have no Icee machines.

12
00:00:33,230 --> 00:00:36,570
Despite my aggressive letter-writing campaign, i might add.

13
00:00:37,130 --> 00:00:39,400
What about the multiplex here? The seats are terrific.

14
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:41,570
They have Twizzlers instead of Red Vines.

15
00:00:41,570 --> 00:00:45,570
No amount of lumbar support can compensate for that.

16
00:00:45,630 --> 00:00:47,850
Well, it's gonna take at least an hour to eat,

17
00:00:47,850 --> 00:00:49,700
and I don't see a Sheldon-approved restaurant

18
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:51,570
proximate to a Sheldon-approved theater.

19
00:00:51,570 --> 00:00:53,490
We could eat after the movie.

20
00:00:53,490 --> 00:00:55,080
Unacceptable.

21
00:00:55,080 --> 00:00:56,080
The delay would result

22
00:00:56,080 --> 00:00:59,580
in tomorrow morning's bowel movement occurring at work.

23
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:02,580
Hang on, hang on. There's a 7-Eleven here.

24
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:05,580
We smuggle Slurpies, which are essentially Icees,

25
00:01:05,580 --> 00:01:06,580
in under our coats,

26
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:10,650
after having a pleasant meal either here, here or here.

27
00:01:10,650 --> 00:01:14,300
Wow. I don't see how we missed that.

28
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:18,310
Excuse me, in what universe are Slurpies Icees?

29
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:22,080
That's how we missed it.

30
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:24,580
Sheldon, would you be prepared, on a non-precedential basis,

31
00:01:24,580 --> 00:01:27,880
to create an emergency ad hoc Slurpie-Icee equivalency?

32
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:30,580
Oh, Leonard, you know I can't do that.

33
00:01:32,810 --> 00:01:34,580
Okay, I guess we only have one option.

34
00:01:34,580 --> 00:01:36,830
Yep, I don't see any way around it.

35
00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:41,210
-Bye, Sheldon. -See ya. -Stay loose.

36
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:49,450
They're right, it was the only option.

37
00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:19,660
Ooh, ooh, shut the door, shut the door.

38
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:21,190
- Why? - Just do it!

39
00:02:25,990 --> 00:02:27,360
Get inside and shut the door

40
00:02:27,430 --> 00:02:28,890
Well, you didn't specify.

41
00:02:31,390 --> 00:02:33,260
Is Leonard around?

42
00:02:33,330 --> 00:02:35,160
He went to the movies without me.

43
00:02:35,230 --> 00:02:36,890
It was the only option.

44
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:49,030
I'm sorry, I don't understand which social situation this is.

45
00:02:49,090 --> 00:02:51,560
Could you give me some guidance as to how to proceed?

46
00:02:51,630 --> 00:02:54,290
The building manager's showing an apartment downstairs,

47
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:56,030
and I haven't paid my rent.

48
00:02:56,090 --> 00:02:58,430
Oh, I see.

49
00:02:58,490 --> 00:03:01,430
Penny, I'm not sure I'm comfortable harboring a fugitive

50
00:03:01,490 --> 00:03:04,090
from the 2311 North Los Robles Corporation.

51
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:06,490
It's no big deal. I'm just a little behind on my bills

52
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:08,360
because they cut back my hours at the restaurant

53
00:03:08,430 --> 00:03:10,130
and my car broke down.

54
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:15,760
If you recall, I pointed out the "check engine" light to you several months ago.

55
00:03:15,830 --> 00:03:20,890
The "check engine" light is fine. It's still blinking away.

56
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:23,590
It's the stupid engine that stopped working.

57
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:26,560
It cost me like $1,200 to fix it.

58
00:03:26,630 --> 00:03:30,190
You know, it occurs to me you could solve all your problems

59
00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:32,930
by obtaining more money.

60
00:03:34,990 --> 00:03:38,290
Yes, it occurs to me, too.

61
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:40,560
Hang on a moment.

62
00:03:50,260 --> 00:03:52,460
Here. Take some.

63
00:03:52,530 --> 00:03:53,990
Pay me back when you can.

64
00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:56,260
Wow, you got a lot of money in there.

65
00:03:56,330 --> 00:03:58,890
That's why it's guarded by snakes.

66
00:04:00,060 --> 00:04:02,260
Take some.

67
00:04:02,330 --> 00:04:03,260
Don't be silly.

68
00:04:03,330 --> 00:04:05,360
I'm never silly.

69
00:04:06,260 --> 00:04:07,490
Here.

70
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:08,790
No, I can't.

71
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:10,260
Don't you need money?

72
00:04:10,330 --> 00:04:12,360
- Well, yeah, but... - This is money I'm not using.

73
00:04:12,430 --> 00:04:13,690
But what if you need it?

74
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:17,590
My expenses account for 46.9% of my after-tax income.

75
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:20,530
The rest is divvied up between a small savings account,

76
00:04:20,590 --> 00:04:23,030
this deceptive container of peanut brittle

77
00:04:23,090 --> 00:04:26,460
and the hollowed-out buttocks of a superhero action figure

78
00:04:26,530 --> 00:04:28,930
who shall remain nameless for his own protection.

79
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:35,160
Or her own protection.

80
00:04:36,730 --> 00:04:38,460
Take some.

81
00:04:38,530 --> 00:04:40,390
Really? I mean, are you sure?

82
00:04:40,460 --> 00:04:42,730
I see no large upcoming expenditures

83
00:04:42,790 --> 00:04:44,360
unless they develop an affordable technology

84
00:04:44,430 --> 00:04:48,560
to fuse my skeleton with adamantium like Wolverine.

85
00:04:48,630 --> 00:04:51,360
Are they working on that?

86
00:04:51,430 --> 00:04:53,760
I sincerely hope so.

87
00:04:55,660 --> 00:04:56,930
Okay.

88
00:04:56,990 --> 00:04:58,990
Well, thank you.

89
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:23,390
Oh, no, I can't. Sheldon honey,

90
00:05:23,460 --> 00:05:26,030
I don't want things to be weird between us.

91
00:05:26,090 --> 00:05:30,730
Won't it also be weird if I have to say hello to you every morning on my way to work

92
00:05:30,790 --> 00:05:34,460
and you're living in a refrigerator box and washing your hair with rain water?

93
00:05:36,030 --> 00:05:37,860
I'll pay you back as soon as I can.

94
00:05:37,930 --> 00:05:39,290
Of course you will.

95
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:42,090
It's impossible to pay me back sooner than you can.

96
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:44,460
Assuming you subscribe

97
00:05:44,530 --> 00:05:47,690
to a linear understanding of time and causality.

98
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:50,560
I'm regretting this already.

99
00:05:53,530 --> 00:05:56,690
You know, I've given the matter some thought,

100
00:05:56,760 --> 00:05:59,360
and I think I'd be willing to be a house pet

101
00:05:59,430 --> 00:06:01,990
to a race of super-intelligent aliens.

102
00:06:02,060 --> 00:06:05,890
Interesting.

103
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:08,030
Ask me why.

104
00:06:08,090 --> 00:06:09,730
Do I have to?

105
00:06:09,790 --> 00:06:10,990
Of course.

106
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:13,090
That's how you move a conversation forward.

107
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:14,860
Why?

108
00:06:14,930 --> 00:06:18,060
The learning opportunities would be abundant.

109
00:06:18,130 --> 00:06:21,360
Additionally, I like having my belly scratched.

110
00:06:23,630 --> 00:06:24,790
Hey, Penny. How was work?

111
00:06:24,860 --> 00:06:26,190
Great.

112
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:28,030
I hope I'm a waitress at the Cheesecake Factory

113
00:06:28,090 --> 00:06:30,060
for my whole life.

114
00:06:30,130 --> 00:06:31,590
Was that sarcasm?

115
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:33,390
No.

116
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:34,760
Was that sarcasm?

117
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:35,890
Yes.

118
00:06:35,990 --> 00:06:39,160
Was that sar-- Stop it!

119
00:06:42,090 --> 00:06:43,460
Penny, you appear to have a package here.

120
00:06:43,530 --> 00:06:44,530
Oh, thanks.

121
00:06:44,590 --> 00:06:46,090
This must be the beret I ordered.

122
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:49,430
A couple of months ago. It was back-ordered.

123
00:06:49,490 --> 00:06:51,690
Did you know the beret is an example

124
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:53,130
of a piece of women's fashion

125
00:06:53,190 --> 00:06:55,190
adapted from male military uniforms?

126
00:06:55,260 --> 00:06:58,590
Another fascinating example is the epaulet.

127
00:07:00,530 --> 00:07:01,890
He's not lying.

128
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:03,830
He does find that fascinating.

129
00:07:03,890 --> 00:07:05,930
Okay, whatever.

130
00:07:05,990 --> 00:07:08,130
It's not like I'm running up and down the streets

131
00:07:08,190 --> 00:07:09,160
just buying myself berets.

132
00:07:09,230 --> 00:07:10,630
I bought one, like, a month ago,

133
00:07:10,690 --> 00:07:11,930
and it was back-ordered.

134
00:07:11,990 --> 00:07:14,190
Look, it finally arrived, all right? All right.

135
00:07:14,260 --> 00:07:16,290
Oh, my God, would you just get off my case?!

136
00:07:18,930 --> 00:07:20,630
Weird.

137
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:23,030
Oh, good, that was an unusual interaction.

138
00:07:23,090 --> 00:07:25,160
I wasn't sure.

139
00:07:25,230 --> 00:07:27,130
Did you guys have an argument?

140
00:07:27,190 --> 00:07:29,330
No.

141
00:07:29,390 --> 00:07:31,960
Well, you clearly did something to aggravate her.

142
00:07:32,030 --> 00:07:33,760
I'm at a loss.

143
00:07:33,830 --> 00:07:37,090
If you like, you can review my daily log of social interactions

144
00:07:37,160 --> 00:07:40,530
and see if there's a blunder I overlooked.

145
00:07:41,860 --> 00:07:43,430
Here you go.

146
00:07:43,490 --> 00:07:44,690
Oh, you owe me another two dollars.

147
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:46,160
The price of moo shu pork went up.

148
00:07:46,230 --> 00:07:50,190
It's getting tougher and tougher to be a bad Jew.

149
00:07:52,130 --> 00:07:54,760
Here you go, Penny. Shrimp with lobster sauce.

150
00:07:54,830 --> 00:07:56,060
Thank you, Leonard. What's my share?

151
00:07:56,130 --> 00:07:58,190
Don't worry about it. It's my treat.

152
00:07:58,260 --> 00:07:59,830
No, really, how much?

153
00:07:59,890 --> 00:08:01,260
It's... whatever. $10, $11.

154
00:08:01,330 --> 00:08:03,160
Well, which is it, $10 or $11?

155
00:08:03,230 --> 00:08:05,330
$14.50. But it's no biggie.

156
00:08:05,390 --> 00:08:07,890
You'll get the next one.

157
00:08:10,730 --> 00:08:11,930
What?

158
00:08:11,990 --> 00:08:14,190
He was just wondering if he wore

159
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:15,860
skintight jeans and a tank top

160
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:19,060
if he'd get his shrimp lo mein for free.

161
00:08:20,330 --> 00:08:21,430
What are you saying?

162
00:08:21,490 --> 00:08:23,860
That I'm using my body to get dinner?

163
00:08:23,930 --> 00:08:26,430
That I'm some kind of Chinese food prostitute?

164
00:08:28,690 --> 00:08:31,860
Yeah, Raj, what are you saying?

165
00:08:31,930 --> 00:08:33,060
'Cause let me tell you something, buddy.

166
00:08:33,130 --> 00:08:34,630
I pay my own way in this world, okay?

167
00:08:34,690 --> 00:08:35,890
I don't rely on anybody!

168
00:08:41,690 --> 00:08:43,190
What was that about?

169
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:47,230
He has a nervous bladder when he's stressed out.

170
00:08:47,290 --> 00:08:50,960
Kind of like a puppy.

171
00:08:51,030 --> 00:08:55,230
Here, Leonard-- $10, $11, $12... $14.

172
00:08:55,290 --> 00:08:58,430
It was $14.50, but it's okay.

173
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:01,090
Oh, good. Dinner's here.

174
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:02,690
Yes, dinner's here, and I'm having some.

175
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:04,030
I'm having takeout food.

176
00:09:04,090 --> 00:09:05,730
Okay. You're damn right it's okay.

177
00:09:05,790 --> 00:09:07,590
I've been having leftovers at the restaurant for like four days,

178
00:09:07,660 --> 00:09:10,130
and I wanted something different. So sue me.

179
00:09:10,190 --> 00:09:11,830
Forgive me, Penny, but that would be

180
00:09:11,890 --> 00:09:14,890
the very definition of a frivolous lawsuit.

181
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:17,360
Sheldon, look, I will pay you back as soon as I can.

182
00:09:17,430 --> 00:09:18,960
You just have to give me more time.

183
00:09:19,030 --> 00:09:20,390
Oh, wait, you lent her money?

184
00:09:20,460 --> 00:09:22,430
She needed money.

185
00:09:22,490 --> 00:09:23,530
You seem under pressure.

186
00:09:23,590 --> 00:09:24,990
Did I not lend you a sufficient amount?

187
00:09:25,060 --> 00:09:26,490
Because I can give you more.

188
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:30,860
Oh, you know, you would just love that, wouldn't you?

189
00:09:30,930 --> 00:09:35,430
Yeah. You would just love to open up your little snake can

190
00:09:35,490 --> 00:09:38,830
and throw some money at the girl who can't pay her bills.

191
00:09:39,990 --> 00:09:40,930
Where are you going?

192
00:09:40,990 --> 00:09:44,190
Going home, where I won't be interrogated like a criminal.

193
00:09:49,430 --> 00:09:51,760
I forgot my fortune cookie.

194
00:09:54,590 --> 00:09:58,360
In case either of you have larceny in your heart,

195
00:09:58,430 --> 00:10:00,660
you should know that I've moved my money out of the snake can.

196
00:10:04,690 --> 00:10:06,090
But if you're ever short,

197
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:09,690
there's always a couple of 50s in Green Lantern's ass.

198
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:23,640
A little mood lighting, huh?

199
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:25,940
When I didn't pay my bill,

200
00:10:26,010 --> 00:10:27,370
the Department of Water and Power thought

201
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:30,040
I would enjoy the ambience.

202
00:10:30,110 --> 00:10:33,640
Yeah, they're very considerate that way.

203
00:10:33,710 --> 00:10:35,770
I used Sheldon's money to pay my rent.

204
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:37,970
Then I had like $14 left over.

205
00:10:38,040 --> 00:10:41,410
$14, huh?

206
00:10:41,470 --> 00:10:42,910
Put it back in your pocket,

207
00:10:42,970 --> 00:10:45,270
or I'll find some other place to put it.

208
00:10:45,340 --> 00:10:48,910
Back in the pocket it goes.

209
00:10:48,970 --> 00:10:53,250
Look, you do understand that Sheldon really doesn't care when he gets the money back.

210
00:10:53,250 --> 00:10:56,370
It's actually one of the few idiosyncrasies that doesn't make you want to,

211
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:58,640
you know, kill him.

212
00:10:58,710 --> 00:11:01,210
Yeah, well, that's not really my big problem.

213
00:11:01,270 --> 00:11:03,040
So you're a little behind on your bills.

214
00:11:03,110 --> 00:11:04,640
Everybody gets behind on their bills.

215
00:11:04,710 --> 00:11:06,970
Yeah, I know, it's just... this wasn't the plan.

216
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:08,970
It wasn't supposed to go this way.

217
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:11,370
Well, what was the plan?

218
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:14,870
Um, waitress for six months and then become a movie star.

219
00:11:18,070 --> 00:11:19,170
Was there a plan B?

220
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:21,240
TV star.

221
00:11:22,770 --> 00:11:24,440
It's probably not as bad as you think.

222
00:11:24,510 --> 00:11:25,470
Let's take a look.

223
00:11:25,540 --> 00:11:28,410
Maybe we can find some corners to cut.

224
00:11:28,470 --> 00:11:30,240
Oh, here's something.

225
00:11:30,310 --> 00:11:31,670
If you don't have electricity,

226
00:11:31,740 --> 00:11:33,770
then you probably don't need cable.

227
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:37,610
Just a suggestion.

228
00:11:40,110 --> 00:11:42,170
$170 dollars for acting classes?

229
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:44,610
Oh, no, I can't give up my acting classes.

230
00:11:44,670 --> 00:11:46,740
I'm a professional actress.

231
00:11:46,810 --> 00:11:48,540
You've had an acting job where you got paid?

232
00:11:48,610 --> 00:11:52,870
That is not the definition of professional.

233
00:11:54,970 --> 00:11:57,970
Actually, it kind of... Let's keep looking.

234
00:12:00,870 --> 00:12:05,740
Whoa, what's $1,800 to the Los Angeles County Superior Court?

235
00:12:05,810 --> 00:12:07,710
Oh, that's nothing.

236
00:12:07,770 --> 00:12:09,110
Nothing?

237
00:12:09,170 --> 00:12:10,840
It sounds like you got caught speeding

238
00:12:10,910 --> 00:12:14,210
going 4,000 miles an hour.

239
00:12:14,270 --> 00:12:15,810
Well, remember Kurt?

240
00:12:15,870 --> 00:12:17,910
Your ex-boyfriend?

241
00:12:17,970 --> 00:12:19,410
Yeah.

242
00:12:19,470 --> 00:12:21,540
He got arrested for taking a whiz on a cop car.

243
00:12:21,610 --> 00:12:22,770
-What? -He was drunk.

244
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:25,610
I would hope so.

245
00:12:25,670 --> 00:12:27,470
Anyway, he had a bunch of outstanding tickets

246
00:12:27,540 --> 00:12:28,510
and a bench warrant,

247
00:12:28,570 --> 00:12:31,070
so I, you know, I paid his fines.

248
00:12:31,140 --> 00:12:32,310
Did he pay you back?

249
00:12:32,370 --> 00:12:33,540
No, but he will.

250
00:12:33,610 --> 00:12:37,340
And that's based on the inherent credit-worthiness of people

251
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:40,940
who get drunk and urinate on police vehicles?

252
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:44,410
Leonard, I'm not gonna call up Kurt and ask him for money.

253
00:12:44,470 --> 00:12:45,640
Well...

254
00:12:45,710 --> 00:12:47,310
what are you gonna do?

255
00:12:47,370 --> 00:12:48,510
I don't know,

256
00:12:48,570 --> 00:12:50,640
but I may have to find a cheaper place to live.

257
00:12:50,710 --> 00:12:53,410
Oh, no...

258
00:12:53,470 --> 00:12:56,110
Oh, you don't want to do that.

259
00:12:56,170 --> 00:12:57,310
Why not?

260
00:12:57,370 --> 00:13:00,070
Moving is a big deal.

261
00:13:00,140 --> 00:13:03,540
You have to go to the supermarket and get boxes,

262
00:13:03,610 --> 00:13:07,110
and if they're not clean, then your books smell like melons,

263
00:13:07,170 --> 00:13:08,270
and it's just, like...

264
00:13:08,910 --> 00:13:11,410
Why don't you just get a roommate and stay here

265
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:13,640
do you know anybody

266
00:13:13,710 --> 00:13:15,840
Well, I'm sure the guy living with Sheldon

267
00:13:15,910 --> 00:13:19,440
wouldn't mind moving in with you.

268
00:13:19,510 --> 00:13:23,870
Oh, Leonard, honey, if we started living together,

269
00:13:23,940 --> 00:13:27,010
I wouldn't be able to keep my hands off you.

270
00:13:28,740 --> 00:13:31,440
Really?

271
00:13:31,510 --> 00:13:34,870
And you thought my acting lessons were a waste of money.

272
00:13:40,670 --> 00:13:44,470
This moo shu pork's burning a hole through my duodenum.

273
00:13:46,110 --> 00:13:48,040
Leviticus 11:3:

274
00:13:48,110 --> 00:13:50,370
"Only that which parteth the hoof and cheweth the cud

275
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:53,840
among the beasts shall ye eat."

276
00:13:53,910 --> 00:13:57,540
Hey, do I mock you with the Bhagavad-Gita every time

277
00:13:57,610 --> 00:13:59,710
you scarf down a Whopper?

278
00:14:04,040 --> 00:14:05,170
Hey, what's going on?

279
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:08,310
We're on a quest through the Valley of Fire to acquire the sacred crown.

280
00:14:08,370 --> 00:14:11,970
You want the Valley of Fire? It's right here.

281
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:15,140
Hey, you guys want to go on a real live quest?

282
00:14:15,210 --> 00:14:17,710
Outside? I just made cocoa.

283
00:14:17,770 --> 00:14:20,210
Come on. It'll be fun.

284
00:14:20,270 --> 00:14:21,110
What is it?

285
00:14:21,170 --> 00:14:24,210
Do you guys remember penny's ex-boyfriend Kurt?

286
00:14:26,810 --> 00:14:28,340
Yeah, that's him.

287
00:14:28,410 --> 00:14:32,210
It turns out he owes Penny a lot of money, and I'm gonna go get it from him.

288
00:14:33,310 --> 00:14:35,440
Who's with me?

289
00:14:38,510 --> 00:14:40,670
Ooh, double sixes.

290
00:14:40,740 --> 00:14:43,340
Really? You're just gonna let me go by myself?

291
00:14:43,410 --> 00:14:45,910
Oh, cool, I got a sword.

292
00:14:45,970 --> 00:14:47,840
I could use some help.

293
00:14:47,910 --> 00:14:49,740
Here.

294
00:14:50,970 --> 00:14:52,770
You guys are unbelievable.

295
00:14:52,840 --> 00:14:54,770
You play a game to simulate adventure,

296
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:58,310
but when there's real adventure out there in the real world, you just wimp out.

297
00:14:58,370 --> 00:15:01,510
Leonard, do you not recall the last time we visited this gentleman,

298
00:15:01,570 --> 00:15:04,270
we returned home without pants?

299
00:15:05,670 --> 00:15:07,210
I do.

300
00:15:07,270 --> 00:15:10,210
Are you sure? Because your proposal suggests that you don't.

301
00:15:10,270 --> 00:15:11,710
I'm not afraid of him.

302
00:15:11,770 --> 00:15:13,910
All right. Leonard fairly calls the question:

303
00:15:13,970 --> 00:15:17,540
Who is in favor of abandoning our game and confronting

304
00:15:17,610 --> 00:15:19,410
Penny's steroid-infused ex-boyfriend

305
00:15:19,470 --> 00:15:23,240
in a suicidal mission to extract money from him?

306
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:27,310
Say hi to Kurt for us.

307
00:15:28,370 --> 00:15:33,110
Excuse me. When Frodo left the Shire to take the one ring to Mordor,

308
00:15:33,170 --> 00:15:35,110
didn't Samwise, Pippin and Merry go with him?

309
00:15:35,170 --> 00:15:36,610
-They did. -Well?

310
00:15:36,670 --> 00:15:39,270
They had a terrible time of it, Leonard.

311
00:15:40,510 --> 00:15:43,610
Plus, no one stole their pants.

312
00:15:43,670 --> 00:15:46,710
Fine. Enjoy your little game.

313
00:15:46,770 --> 00:15:48,970
I'll make this quest on my own.

314
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:49,870
Leonard, wait.

315
00:15:50,970 --> 00:15:51,910
Take a jacket.

316
00:15:51,970 --> 00:15:53,610
It's shpritzing a little.

317
00:15:53,670 --> 00:15:55,310
You guys suck.

318
00:15:59,110 --> 00:16:01,410
Come on, please? He's so big.

319
00:16:03,670 --> 00:16:05,870
Okay, is everyone clear on the plan?

320
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:07,970
Yes. Koothrappali's going to wet himself,

321
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:10,110
I'm gonna throw up, Sheldon's gonna run away,

322
00:16:10,170 --> 00:16:12,240
and you're going to die.

323
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:15,770
Shall we synchronize our watches?

324
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:18,440
Guys, there are four of us and one of him.

325
00:16:18,510 --> 00:16:21,510
Which means his triumph will be even larger.

326
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:25,140
Minstrels will write songs about him.

327
00:16:25,210 --> 00:16:26,240
Okay, how about this?

328
00:16:26,310 --> 00:16:27,540
I'll do the talking.

329
00:16:27,610 --> 00:16:30,410
You just stand behind me and try to look formidable.

330
00:16:36,110 --> 00:16:38,370
I should've peed before we left.

331
00:16:39,610 --> 00:16:41,340
Yeah?

332
00:16:44,940 --> 00:16:45,870
Hi, Kurt.

333
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:47,210
Lenny, right?

334
00:16:47,270 --> 00:16:49,640
I don't really go by Lenny, but that's okay.

335
00:16:49,710 --> 00:16:51,970
Um, you remember

336
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:53,870
Sheldon, Howard and Raj.

337
00:16:53,940 --> 00:16:57,170
No. What do you want?

338
00:16:57,240 --> 00:16:58,540
He don't remember me?

339
00:16:58,610 --> 00:16:59,910
How could he not remember me?

340
00:16:59,970 --> 00:17:00,810
Sheldon, not now.

341
00:17:00,870 --> 00:17:03,210
I remember him.

342
00:17:03,270 --> 00:17:05,940
Okay, here it is. Penny's in kind of a financial jam,

343
00:17:06,010 --> 00:17:08,570
and the money that you owe her would go a long way

344
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:09,740
to solving her problems.

345
00:17:09,810 --> 00:17:11,570
And she sent you to get it from me?

346
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:14,370
No, no, she's too proud to ask for the money.

347
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:17,240
I, on the other hand, feel you should honor your debt.

348
00:17:17,310 --> 00:17:18,940
You do?

349
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:24,870
"Feel" is a kind of a... it's a strong word.

350
00:17:24,940 --> 00:17:27,840
Um, I just think it would be a nice gesture on your part.

351
00:17:27,910 --> 00:17:29,510
She'll get it when she gets it.

352
00:17:34,070 --> 00:17:38,170
Well, there you go. Problem solved.

353
00:17:38,240 --> 00:17:39,770
A successful quest.

354
00:17:39,840 --> 00:17:41,870
Now let's go find a gas station with a clean bathroom.

355
00:17:41,940 --> 00:17:44,470
No, the problem isn't solved.

356
00:17:44,540 --> 00:17:45,740
He just blew us off.

357
00:17:45,810 --> 00:17:47,810
I've got it.

358
00:17:47,870 --> 00:17:50,140
He didn't remember me because the last time we met,

359
00:17:50,210 --> 00:17:52,640
I was in a Halloween costume.

360
00:17:53,840 --> 00:17:55,740
Come on, Leonard, let's go.

361
00:17:55,810 --> 00:17:57,170
No. You can leave if you want to.

362
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:58,310
I'm gonna see this through.

363
00:17:58,370 --> 00:18:00,210
Okay.

364
00:18:05,870 --> 00:18:08,470
I guess, technically, that was my fault.

365
00:18:14,870 --> 00:18:16,470
I'm not leaving here without Penny's money.

366
00:18:16,540 --> 00:18:19,310
What happened to your backup?

367
00:18:20,870 --> 00:18:22,270
I don't need backup.

368
00:18:22,340 --> 00:18:24,570
I have right on my side.

369
00:18:28,170 --> 00:18:33,140
And I'm wearing cargo shorts under my pants.

370
00:18:34,510 --> 00:18:36,510
congratulations.

371
00:18:36,570 --> 00:18:38,710
You may not have succeeded in getting cash,

372
00:18:38,770 --> 00:18:42,040
but you did secure a formal acknowledgment of the debt.

373
00:18:47,110 --> 00:18:49,840
Maybe we should have your head notarized.

374
00:18:51,840 --> 00:18:55,950
If anybody cares, I still have to pee

375
00:19:06,070 --> 00:19:07,840
-Hey. Is Sheldon here? -Yeah. Hang on.

376
00:19:07,910 --> 00:19:09,140
Sheldon!

377
00:19:09,210 --> 00:19:10,840
Nice hat.

378
00:19:10,910 --> 00:19:14,240
It's kind of a fashionable look these days.

379
00:19:14,310 --> 00:19:17,370
Maybe if you're working on a tuna boat.

380
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:18,870
Hello, Penny.

381
00:19:18,940 --> 00:19:20,270
Sheldon, here is your money.

382
00:19:20,340 --> 00:19:22,370
Thank you very much. It helped a lot.

383
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:25,040
Sarcasm?

384
00:19:25,110 --> 00:19:26,370
No.

385
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:29,010
Darn. I can't seem to get the hang of that.

386
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:31,540
Hey, I know it's none of my business,

387
00:19:31,610 --> 00:19:33,370
but where did the money come from?

388
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:35,840
Well, I cut back my expenses like you said

389
00:19:35,910 --> 00:19:38,010
and picked up a few more hours at the restaurant,

390
00:19:38,070 --> 00:19:39,710
but the biggest thing was, out of the blue,

391
00:19:39,770 --> 00:19:40,740
Kurt shows up

392
00:19:40,810 --> 00:19:42,610
and gives me the money he owes me..

393
00:19:42,670 --> 00:19:47,470
Really? Did he say why?

394
00:19:47,540 --> 00:19:50,240
Yes, he said he was feeling guilty

395
00:19:50,310 --> 00:19:51,740
and wanted to do what was right.

396
00:19:53,710 --> 00:19:56,610
That's it?

397
00:19:57,810 --> 00:20:02,840
Did he give any reason as to why he came to this moral epiphany?

398
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:06,540
Nope. I just think he's really changed.

399
00:20:08,840 --> 00:20:10,140
We're having dinner tomorrow night,

400
00:20:10,210 --> 00:20:12,140
and I get to wear my new beret.

401
00:20:12,210 --> 00:20:14,610
Bye, guys.

402
00:20:14,670 --> 00:20:16,570
Bye.

403
00:20:20,070 --> 00:20:23,340
Well done, Leonard.

404
00:20:24,470 --> 00:20:27,340
The true hero doesn't seek adulation.

405
00:20:27,410 --> 00:20:29,670
He fights for right and justice simply

406
00:20:29,670 --> 00:20:30,870
because it's his nature.

407
00:20:30,940 --> 00:20:34,170
Penny's hooking up with her jerk of an ex-boyfriend,

408
00:20:34,240 --> 00:20:37,170
and I have indelible ink on my forehead!

409
00:20:37,240 --> 00:20:38,570
That's your badge of honor

410
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:41,510
your warrior's wound, if you will.

411
00:20:41,570 --> 00:20:43,210
I was wrong.

412
00:20:43,270 --> 00:20:46,410
Minstrels will write songs about you.

413
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:48,810
Great.

414
00:20:49,530 --> 00:20:53,930
* There once was a brave lad named Leonard *

415
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,470
* With a fi-fi fiddle dee-dee *

416
00:20:56,530 --> 00:20:59,000
* He faced a fearsome giant *

417
00:20:59,070 --> 00:21:03,190
* While Raj just wanted to pee. *

